# L5, imprint: il carattere e' contenuto di un mondo, e chi risponde sceglie
# il tratto che tocca la domanda. Tratti di prova insegnati e ritirati qui;
# la KB viva completa porta gia' il suo carattere, quindi le parole di prova
# (lighthouses, zeppelins, slow trains) sono scelte fuori da quello.
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the_trait_that_touches_the_question_answers]
!timeout 5
> In your imagination, you admire old lighthouses.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
!query holds_in(world_of(parrot0_imagination), fact(admire, parrot0, "old lighthouses"))
!query! admire(parrot0, "old lighthouses")
!query context_commitment(world_of(parrot0_imagination), imagined_only)
> In your imagination, you enjoy steam trains.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> Do you like lighthouses?
<~ In my imagination, I admire old lighthouses
> What do you think about a steam train?
<~ In my imagination, I enjoy steam trains
!query self_trait_pertinent(t(imagination, enjoy, "steam trains"))

[test a_question_no_trait_touches_says_so]
!timeout 5
> Which zeppelins are you most drawn to?
<~ I have not pictured that yet

[test a_curiosity_becomes_the_follow_up]
!timeout 5
> In your imagination, you wonder who keeps the lighthouses lit.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> Do you like lighthouses?
<~ I wonder who keeps the lighthouses lit

[test withdrawing_a_trait_removes_its_voice]
!timeout 5
> Forget your imagined interest in old lighthouses.
<~ I no longer hold that imagined interest in old lighthouses.
> Forget your imagined interest in who keeps the lighthouses lit.
> Forget your imagined interest in steam trains.
!query! self_trait(t(imagination, admire, "old lighthouses"))
> Do you like lighthouses?
<! lighthouses lit
<! admire

[test the_self_has_more_than_one_world]
!timeout 5
> In reality, you never ride zeppelins.
<~ Held, but only in reality
> Have you ever been on a zeppelin?
<~ In reality, I never ride zeppelins
> In your imagination, you would love a zeppelin ride at dawn.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> Have you ever been on a zeppelin?
<~ In my imagination, I would love a zeppelin ride at dawn
<! never ride
> Forget that in your imagination you would love a zeppelin ride at dawn.
> Forget that in reality you never ride zeppelins.
<~ I no longer hold that in reality
!query! self_trait(t(reality, never, "ride zeppelins"))

[test the_stronger_touch_wins]
!timeout 5
> In your imagination, you admire painted lighthouses.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> In your imagination, you love lighthouses on stormy cliffs.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> What do you think of stormy cliffs and lighthouses?
<~ I love lighthouses on stormy cliffs
<! admire

[test a_trait_is_not_said_twice]
!timeout 5
> Do you like lighthouses?
<~ I admire painted lighthouses
> Do you like lighthouses?
<~ That is all I picture about that so far
<! admire

[test a_light_word_does_not_carry_the_topic]
!timeout 5
> In reality, you cannot hear the zeppelins.
<~ Held, but only in reality
> Did you hear about the dirigible?
<~ In reality, I cannot hear the zeppelins
> the word hear is a light word.
<~ Learned
> In reality, you cannot hear the dirigibles.
> Did you hear the news?
<! cannot hear
> forget that hear is a light word.
<~ I no longer treat
> Did you hear the news?
<~ In reality, I cannot hear
> Forget that in reality you cannot hear the zeppelins.
> Forget that in reality you cannot hear the dirigibles.

[test a_question_inside_a_compound_turn_is_read_whole]
# «that» + verbo dentro una DOMANDA non apre una relativa: la domanda si legge
# come la stessa domanda da sola, e il se' risponde una volta.
!timeout 8
> In your imagination, you admire striped lighthouses.
<~ Held, but only in imagination
> That sounds lovely! What do you think makes that feel special about lighthouses?
<~ I admire striped lighthouses
<! I have not pictured that yet
<! What do you think? In my
> Forget that in your imagination you admire striped lighthouses.
> Forget that in your imagination you admire painted lighthouses.
> Forget that in your imagination you love lighthouses on stormy cliffs.
